    "notes": [
      "Colour is displacement magnitude, not a failure warning. The fixed 0\u20131 mm scale above makes different loads easier to compare.",
      "A 2 kg object at 130 mm adds 19.61 N downward and 2.55 N\u00b7m of turning moment at the rail. A corner position also adds 1.27 N\u00b7m across the shelf width.",
      "Opposing contact forces can each exceed the object\u2019s weight: they form a couple over a short separation to resist the turning moment. Their vector sum still balances the applied weight.",
      "The rail transfers the resultant force and moment through the frame and legs to the floor. We have not calculated stress or deflection in the table itself.",
      "Your confirmed real-world fit takes precedence over the downloaded table mesh. Its approximately 10 mm rim is not used for the contact calculation. Any small real clearance or friction remains outside this nominal model.",
      "Numerical contact check: multiplying the penalty stiffness by four changed maximum movement by -0.41%.",
      "Mesh check for front 2 kg: refining from 2 mm to 1.25 mm changed maximum movement by -6.21% (0.406 to 0.381 mm). This single refinement does not establish full convergence or peak-stress accuracy."
